nzymes  would actually degrade these bacteria  that's how this threat is eliminated  but in sharia highgasses syndrome due to  a defective lysos  defective least gene product  the trafficking  of substances in the lysosome is  defective  and one of the implication is the  lysosome cannot  fuse with the endosome and the  phagolysosome cannot be formed  now that is why  bacteriolysis could not occur  and this affects several cell types  especially  the phagocytotic cells of the immune  system such as dendritic cell and the  macrophages whenever  bacteria or virus invaded our body  macrophage and the dendritic cell try to  engulf that pathogen  with by the process of phagocytosis  and inside  the phagosome  lysosome actually fuse with these  endosomes and ultimately creates  phagolysosome where the bacterias are  dead  by the harsh lysosomal enzymes so  bacteriolysis can take place  but in cheria higas syndrome due to this  faulty least gene product this  fusion of lysosome and the endosome does  not take place as a result there is no  bacteriolysis and body is more and more  susceptible  to  bacterial infection  another cell type which is highly  affected due to this mutation is the  cytotoxic c  t cells  cytotoxic t cells can secrete specific  uh  granules which are known as  perforin and granzymes  this can actually demolish  the cells which are infected by virus  especially that induce  apoptotic pathway so ultimately the cell  dies  and that is how cytodoxic t cell work  but in this list gene mutant these  granules can not actually be secreted  properly  and as a result  body is more susceptible to viral  infection as well  in shedding hygasi syndrome one of the  important thing that we see  frequent bruising on the skin  and  sometimes even bleeding because the  platelets are also affected in these  in this genetic situation where list  gene is mutated  that is why we see frequent bruising and  sometimes even bleeding which is a kind  of severe  now another impli